@startuml
title UML Component Overview — AIOS Service Boundaries
left to right direction
skinparam componentStyle uml1
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultFontName Arial
skinparam defaultFontSize 15
component "Telemetry Collector\nCPU / RAM / I/O / PSI" as Collector
component "AI Inference Service\nmodel boundary TBD" as Inference
component "Decision & Policy Service\nper-process gates" as Policy
component "Safety Watchdog\ninhibit / recovery" as Watchdog
component "Resource Manager / Actuator\nonly proposed host writer" as Actuator
component "Read-only Dashboard API" as Dashboard
database "Telemetry & Read-Projection Store\nSQLite" as Telemetry
database "Audit Store\nseparate SQLite" as Audit
node "Linux host interfaces\nprocfs / PSI / cgroups v2" as Host
interface "IInference" as IInference
interface "ITelemetryRead" as ITelemetryRead
interface "ITelemetryStoreWrite" as ITelemetryStoreWrite
interface "IActionRequest / IActionOutcome" as IAction
interface "IResourceControl" as IControl
Collector ..> ITelemetryStoreWrite : writes accepted samples
ITelemetryStoreWrite -- Telemetry
Inference ..> ITelemetryRead : reads bounded evidence
ITelemetryRead -- Telemetry
Policy ..> IInference : requests prediction
IInference -- Inference
Policy ..> IAction : submits gated action
IAction -- Actuator
Actuator ..> IControl : applies and verifies
IControl -- Host
Collector ..> Host : reads telemetry
Watchdog ..> Policy : inhibits new proposals
Watchdog ..> Actuator : requests guarded recovery
Policy ..> Audit : appends decision evidence
Actuator ..> Audit : appends action evidence
Dashboard ..> Telemetry : read-only projections
Dashboard ..> Audit : read-only audit summary
note bottom
All controls are proposed. CPU, RAM, and I/O have separate capability and bounds checks; the dashboard has no write interface.
@enduml
